% Bibliography for "Aggregate Accuracy Conceals an Acquisition-Level Failure
% in a Public Radar Target Recognition Benchmark".
%
% Keys match the \cite commands already in paper_main.tex, so switching from
% the manual thebibliography to this file changes no citation in the text.
%
% Author names are given as initials, exactly as the manually typed
% bibliography carried them. Expanding them to full first names would mean
% guessing, and a guessed first name in a reference list is a fabrication
% that survives into every paper that cites yours. If you want them
% expanded, take the full names from each paper's own title page rather
% than from anyone's recollection.
%
% Accents are written as LaTeX escapes rather than UTF-8, which keeps the
% file safe under both bibtex and a toolchain that has not been told the
% input encoding. Braces around DopplerNet, RAD-DAR, CNN, UAV and Doppler
% are deliberate: IEEEtran lowercases titles, and without them those words
% come out wrong.
%
% Each DOI appears twice, in doi and again in note. IEEEtran.bst 1.14 has no
% support for the doi field and silently drops it, which would have quietly
% lost every DOI the manually typed bibliography carried. The note field is
% rendered by every style, so the DOI survives whichever one a venue
% requires. The doi field is kept because other styles do use it.

